#718: the #714 statement profile re-run, with the writer-lock accounting this
issue added alongside it. Same methodology and the same command as
bench/results/2026-08-11-tpcc-stmt-profile-granary.csv, so the per-statement
tables are directly comparable row for row:

  GRANARY_TPCC_WAREHOUSES=1, GRANARY_TPCC_TERMINALS=1,
  GRANARY_TPCC_SECONDS=10, GRANARY_TPCC_WARMUP_SECONDS=2,
  GRANARY_TPCC_ENGINES=granary, GRANARY_TPC_SEED=42 (default),
  GRANARY_TPCC_STMT_PROFILE=1, GRANARY_TPCC_STMT_PROFILE_CSV=bench/results.

One bench_tpcc.exe run, not repeated or averaged. Measured interval 10.041 s,
28.385 NewOrder/sec, 99.6-100.0% of every profile's service time attributed.
The pre/post consistency oracle reported "ok" on both sides (conditions 1-4),
which at TERMINALS=1 is expected rather than informative -- #706's race needs a
second handle.

Host: containerized dev image (granary-dev) on an 8-core Intel i7-8650U
laptop, load average 1.6-2.6 at launch (sibling work running).

WHAT MAY AND MAY NOT BE COMPARED WITH THE 2026-08-11 RUN

The two runs are on DIFFERENT HOSTS. The 2026-08-11 file carries no .meta
recording its machine, and this one was produced on a laptop, so:

- The throughput headline is NOT comparable. 28.385 NewOrder/sec here against
  32.957 on 2026-08-11 says nothing about #717; do not read it as a
  regression, and do not read it as a win either.
- The ROLLBACK per-call figure IS comparable, and is the point of the re-run:
  358.9164 ms/call (4 calls, 25.72% of new_order) -> 0.485 ms/call (3 calls,
  0.03%). That is 740x on a per-operation latency whose asymptotics changed
  from a full tree drain to a root-to-leaf descent (#717) on a ~300k-row
  order_line. No host difference reaches two orders of magnitude, and the two
  runs load the same W=1 population from the same seed for the same 10 s.

The lock tables (the last three in the CSV) have no counterpart in the
2026-08-11 file -- nothing in the tree could produce them before #718.

  site            acquires  contend    wait_ms   hold_ms
  txn                  670       60   2515.531  7504.567
  autocheckpoint        60        0      0.019  2519.228
  checkpoint             0        0      0.000     0.000
  commit_sink            0        0      0.000     0.000
  txn blocked by autocheckpoint: 60 waits, 2515.353 ms
  unattributed_waits 0, unbalanced_releases 0

unattributed_waits = 0 over 730 acquisitions is the funnel invariant holding
under a real workload: no acquisition of the writer lock bypassed the
accounting, so the two tables above are complete and not merely plausible.
